{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385305-hunting-the-moon","id":1385305,"title":"Hunting the Moon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-02T14:48:09-07:00","id":1385305,"title":"Hunting the Moon","content":"So I'm running a game where an invading Prasadi legion has become aware of at least two maybe more lunars operating in the area. What are tricks (mundane or magical, sorcerous or charms) that a millitary can use to mitigate the chances of infiltration or damage, if they know the Lunars are out there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T15:27:30-07:00","id":1385310,"title":"","content":"Tighten patrols and use things like passwords and code-phrases, to make sure that someone doesn't just look like a friendly - but is a friendly<br /> <br /> Similarly, dig out their encampments so that even animals can't sneap up on them. Basically just dig and stamp the dirt around the camp, erect wooden palisades, keep everything well lit at night and have regular patrols.<br /> <br /> Anyone who's important gets lots of bodyguards, so they're never alone to be nommed and body-swapped by a lunar<br /> <br /> In 2nd ed there were these artifacts called &quot;Essence flare pillars&quot; - they could be used to force anyone who walks within their area of effect (maximum of 200 yard squad) to blow 16 motes and go full iconic anima. Great way to forcibly reveal a hidden exalt. This would be perfect to have the main gates to an army camp, where everyone has to pass through - but also perhaps hidden around an army camp, around the officers tent area perhaps.<br /> <br /> means of bestowing essence sight to mortals for guard duty would be good - if your game has stuff like that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T01:20:50-07:00","id":1385377,"title":"","content":"Be Upright Soldiers.<br /> <br /> No-one goes anywhere alone. Or in pairs. You go in your Fang of five.<br /> <br /> Standard military discipline. Passphrases.<br /> <br /> Everyone digs their own grave ahead of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T04:33:55-07:00","id":1385384,"title":"","content":"keeping the newer members of the legion under extra close watch, have the veterans report any odd behavior displayed by their tent mates (I'm guessing that the legions use the roman style of I believe it was ten men per tent that form closer ties to each other).<br /> Have soldiers give each other trick questions like &quot;hows you're wife?&quot; other individual answers &quot;oh she's fine!&quot; and that can indicate that they are fake if said character is unmarried.<br /> Having suspects stay out under the full moon then put them under extra stress to see if the lunar will fall to their provocations (since I'm pretty sure that the moon madness of the Lunars ought to be pretty common knowledge for the dragon-blooded legions).<br /> <br /> Another could be to injure the highly suspected individuals.<br /> They will heal faster so give them an injury then have them report to the medics the next day and if it's healed then they are about 90% confirmed as a Lunar.<br /> <br /> One last trick would be fake decimation.<br /> Every ten soldier (including officers) are sentenced to be beaten to death by their tent mates.<br /> Make sure that the suspects are picked.<br /> At this point the Lunar has to reveal itself or die, but it can put some serious strain on the soldiers trust of their leadership and will not work again if you don't follow through with it which would deal severe damage to the legion.<br /> <br /> That's a few of the tricks I have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T05:27:47-07:00","id":1385390,"title":"","content":"Moon madness isn\u2019t a thing in 3E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T05:34:54-07:00","id":1385391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385305-hunting-the-moon?p=1385390#post1385390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moon madness isn\u2019t a thing in 3E.</div> </div> </div> </div>well that's one trick gone...<br /> I guess I'll have to wait for the pdf before I learn what else has changed...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T10:44:04-07:00","id":1385430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385305-hunting-the-moon?p=1385391#post1385391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well that's one trick gone...<br /> I guess I'll have to wait for the pdf before I learn what else has changed...</div> </div> </div> </div>If memory serves, it\u2019s not too late to retroactively back the Kickstarter via BackerKit, at least, to get PDF access.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T12:43:32-07:00","id":1385446,"title":"","content":"I wrote this a while back <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Tips for Wyld Hunting Lunars</span><br /> <ul><li>When the Astrologers tell you of the appearance of a new Anathema, make haste. The Ogres amongst the Anathema use their profane magics to learn of these new Moon Mad and send forth their minions to capture them, so it is imperative to get there quickly.</li> <li>Knowledge is key. All Silver Anathema have an identifying mark upon their bodies that cannot be altered, the Tell, so it is paramount to watch for this, but do not discount any other information that can be gleaned. The demon often retains the memories and some of the relationships held by their host body for a time after possession. These ties can be used to lure out the Anathema from their lair, to determine their likely habits and strategies, and what goals they might initially pursue. However, be forewarned. The warping that occurs when the demon takes a new host is most severe in the Silver Anathema, such that the final demon may not retain anything of the original host, not in body, mind, or soul.</li> <li>Nearly every Wyld Hunt that has pursued a Silver Anathema has lost it at one point or another. Do not think of this as failure, but as another opportunity to learn. Most young Moon Mad instinctively know to steal the form of a bird or fish as soon as they can, but most only gain one form. When they change, watch their new form as much as you can, both to learn its markings and to see their Tell. This will help you to take them down a second time.</li> <li>Practice hunting. Learn to track, hunt, and kill every animal under the sun, so that you cannot be surprised later. Learn the habits of animals, such that you may spot them acting strangely or flush them out depriving the Anathema of their concealment.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T12:50:00-07:00","id":1385447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385305-hunting-the-moon?p=1385430#post1385430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If memory serves, it\u2019s not too late to retroactively back the Kickstarter via BackerKit, at least, to get PDF access.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think you get retroactive access to the Kickstarter manuscript via backerkit. However, the Lunars book is currently in proofing so they should have a backer copy out to people pretty soon. After that, they usually give a month for errata collection and then another couple months to fix everything before releasing it to the general public.<br /> <br /> If you can still go through backerkit, that should get you the backer copy when it arrives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T23:37:49-07:00","id":1385550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385305-hunting-the-moon?p=1385430#post1385430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If memory serves, it\u2019s not too late to retroactively back the Kickstarter via BackerKit, at least, to get PDF access.</div> </div> </div> </div>already have, just waiting for it to be finished.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T23:58:32-07:00","id":1385552,"title":"","content":"I mean, Brilliant Rain has the right of it. Their suggestion has covered more or less what rank and file Deebs would know, or think they know about Lunar capabilities.<br /> <br /> When you get the manuscript, you'll see that its just scratching the surface of Lunar dickery, of course, but by the time the ant under the floorboard has Cantata of Empty Voices-ed your army to death, it would be too late to revise the training manual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T00:21:36-07:00","id":1385555,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s also theoretically spells/charms and demons and artifacts that aren\u2019t published but may exist. Even as just a one off or a rare few if the General always dines in front of a mirror that reveals the true form of shapeshifters or something that would go a long way.<br /> <br /> The Realm\u2019s greatest strength is in its military might, and obviously the Silver Pact has issues dealing with it, otherwise the Shogunate would have been destroyed never mind the Realm. So basically just tune up the powers of the Realm\u2019s artifacts and Exalted to the point where they stand a reasonable chance of not having every general they ever send out killed and replaced by a Lunar, but also not so incredible that they can\u2019t ever have that happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T01:03:37-07:00","id":1385558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385305-hunting-the-moon?p=1385552#post1385552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you get the manuscript, you'll see that its just scratching the surface of Lunar dickery, of course, but by the time the ant under the floorboard has Cantata of Empty Voices-ed your army to death, it would be too late to revise the training manual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is something stopping the army from just leaving in this hypothetical?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T01:23:07-07:00","id":1385559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385305-hunting-the-moon?p=1385558#post1385558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is something stopping the army from just leaving in this hypothetical?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar speed and stealth charms? Said ant could also be a flea in a saddle pack, a moth fluttering on a tent roof or a weevil infesting the grain seized from hapless villagers. <br /> <br /> All the while, travelling with the army, singing that murderous tune through the wee hours of the night.<br /> <br /> Edit: The alternative is the Sorcerous Raptor in the sky who from Extreme range (just a mote on the horizon!) launches Flight of the Brilliant Raptor continuously until everything for a league around gets burnt to a crisp.<br /> <br /> That works too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 05-04-2020, 04:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T01:33:10-07:00","id":1385560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385305-hunting-the-moon?p=1385559#post1385559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar speed and stealth charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Once the source of a sound is discerned, people can move away from it. And I don't recall anything in Cantata of Empty Voices saying that the obvious glowing singing wraiths are hidden because the caster is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385305-hunting-the-moon?p=1385559#post1385559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The alternative is the Sorcerous Raptor in the sky who from Extreme range l(just a speck!) aunches Flight of the Brilliant Raptor until everything for a league around gets burnt to a crisp.<br /> <br /> That works too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but how's that meaningfully different from a Dragon-Blooded or even mortal sorcerer atop a Cirrus Skiff sniping from extreme range? <i>Just a speck!</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T01:43:28-07:00","id":1385561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385305-hunting-the-moon?p=1385560#post1385560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once the source of a sound is discerned, people can move away from it. And I don't recall anything in Cantata of Empty Voices saying that the obvious glowing singing wraiths are hidden because the caster is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the idea is just to start late at night when most are asleep, cause a Wing or three to asphyxiate and then go switch form and hide somewhere while they are panicking? Then just ride along with their hurried retreat and repeat the next night, maybe skip a night to lull them into a false sense of security and then do it again?<br /> <br /> I mean, I\u2019m not an infiltration genius or anything, but even I can see that that would be devastating and hard to deal with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, but how's that meaningfully different from a Dragon-Blooded or even mortal sorcerer atop a Cirrus Skiff sniping from extreme range? <i>Just a speck!</i> </div> </div> </div>Mostly the pair of success-eating stealth dice that you have in small form and the inability to have your ride be distorted?<br /> <br /> Edit: Though we are rather gumming up the good OPs page, so I suggest we halt the escalation before Dragonblooded Kong Ming and Lunar Hanzo Hasashi get wheeled out. <br /> <br /> The release of Lunars will be soon enough and he can decide for himself which of us has the right of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 05-04-2020, 04:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T02:09:50-07:00","id":1385562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385305-hunting-the-moon?p=1385561#post1385561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean the idea is just to start late at night when most are asleep, cause a Wing or three to asphyxiate and then go switch form and hide somewhere while they are panicking?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think <i>three wings of soldiers</i> sleep inside a single short range band?<br /> <br /> \u200bRemember, the damage on Cantata of Empty Voices is 2L, and lasts only as long as you're sustaining it. In order to even threaten to kill a single soldier, you'll have to be standing next to him for a minimum of four turns. Four turns in which <b>you are outlined by shrieking spirits that follow you if you move</b>. You're not going to get to &quot;ride along with their hurried retreat.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385305-hunting-the-moon?p=1385561#post1385561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I\u2019m not an infiltration genius or anything, but even I can see that that would be devastating and hard to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why don't you try dicing this out before you go suggesting it as a tactic?<br /> <br /> \u200bI just got through with a game session in which we fought a sorcerer who had a Charm that let him use Cantata of Empty Voices each turn and still take his combat action. His head got ripped off his neck.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385305-hunting-the-moon?p=1385561#post1385561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though we are rather gumming up the good OPs page, so I suggest we halt the escalation before Dragonblooded Kong Ming and Lunar Hanzo Hasashi get wheeled out.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you sincerely believe you're dragging a discussion off-topic, please don't continue the argument <i>before</i> suggesting that the argument be halted. Even if it's not your intent, it makes it read as disingenuous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-04-2020, 05:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T04:24:29-07:00","id":1385581,"title":"","content":"I do have the Lunar Manuscript, don't worry so much about that. The feedback has been very helpful, as has some I've gotten elsewhere of trying to lure a lunar into a trap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T05:42:24-07:00","id":1385594,"title":"","content":"Are the Lunars involved players or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T06:39:09-07:00","id":1385600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385305-hunting-the-moon?p=1385594#post1385594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the Lunars involved players or not?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They are not, although player lunars may get involved. In my case, it's an E3 lunar and an E5 Lunar pair of NPCs. The Dragonblooded are aware at least one Lunar is an experienced elder (the E5).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T17:38:19-07:00","id":1386215,"title":"","content":"Lunars fight using guerrilla tactics and lightning raids mostly. This is for two reasons:<br /> <br /> 1) Lunars can afford to play the long game.<br /> 2) Lunars are actually pretty rare, Elders even more so.<br /> <br /> There are only 400 Lunars in Creation and elders who are several hundred years old form a fairly tiny percentage of that number. I\u2019m not going to say that such beings are all infallible masterminds, but they are likely to, ya know, not going to want to die and, historically, using hit and run tactics have the best chance of success without dying. In any case, a Lunar is likely to want to cut and run the moment they get hurt or things go badly... unless there\u2019s something they need to remain to handle, something more important than their own safety.<br /> <br /> Adding some intimacies that the players can learn about and use as bait to draw out and trap the lunar could be fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}